//RS //! D-DEV3 save-to-diagnostic latency budget, measured with nothing else running.
//RS //!
//RS //! Card #2005. This assertion used to live in `tests/dev.rs`, sharing one
//RS //! process with the rest of the dev suite. Wall clock there reports scheduler
//RS //! contention as much as compiler work: the same commit failed in the full
//RS //! parallel run and passed under `--test-threads=1 --exact`, and the verdict
//RS //! moved when the suite grew by 32 reached tests without the front end
//RS //! changing at all. A verdict that moves with the suite's size is not a
//RS //! latency detector.
//RS //!
//RS //! D-DEV3 is a wall-clock promise to the user — "a save gives feedback in well
//RS //! under 200ms" (`Docs/spec/diagnostics.md`) — so the measurement basis stays
//RS //! wall clock and the budget stays 200ms. What changed is where it is
//RS //! measured. This file is its own cargo test target holding exactly one test,
//RS //! and both `cargo test` and `Tools/ci/test-shards.sh` run one target per
//RS //! process, one after another. So nothing else in the run is executing while
//RS //! the number is taken, and the count of tests elsewhere cannot move it.
//RS //!
//RS //! It still catches the regression the budget exists for. The measured round is
//RS //! the same front-end check the watch loop performs on every save, so any
//RS //! change that pushes it past 200ms — a slower parse, a standard-library
//RS //! re-read per check, a quadratic sema walk, a newly blocking lookup — fails
//RS //! here.
//RS //!
//RS //! Two alternatives were considered and rejected. Counting work (steps, bytes)
//RS //! instead of time needs a machine-specific steps-to-milliseconds constant
//RS //! before it can say anything about the 200ms promise, and it stays green
//RS //! through a regression that spends its time blocking rather than computing. A
//RS //! ratio against a same-run baseline check cancels fixed per-save cost, since
//RS //! both sides pay it — and fixed per-save cost is exactly what D-DEV3 bounds.
//RS 
//RS /// The example whose per-save round is measured.
//RS const EXAMPLE: &str = "Examples/features/collections/wordcount.jet";
//RS 
//RS /// The D-DEV3 budget for one check-only save-to-diagnostic round, in
//RS /// milliseconds. Never widen this to make a run agree: a trip is a latency
//RS /// defect to report, not a limit to raise.
//RS const BUDGET_MS: u128 = 200;
//RS 
//RS /// Rounds timed after the warm-up. The best of them is the sample least
//RS /// disturbed by anything outside this process.
//RS const ROUNDS: usize = 5;
//RS const WATCH_LATENCY_MARGIN_MS: u128 = 20;
//RS 
//RS /// Measure the shared watcher itself, separately from front-end work. The
//RS /// bound is derived from the configured coalescing window rather than widened
//RS /// to make a slow implementation pass.
